        "articleNumber": "10190652",
        "articleTitle": "Who owns this code? Examining Ownership Concepts in InnerSource Practices",
        "volume": null,
        "issue": null,
        "startPage": "2",
        "endPage": "3",
        "publisher": "IEEE",
        "articleContentType": "Conferences",
        "publicationTitle": "2023 IEEE/ACM 1st International Workshop on InnerSource Software Development (InnerSoft)",
        "authors": [
            {
                "id": 37089922790,
                "preferredName": "Clare Dillon",
                "firstName": "Clare",
                "lastName": "Dillon"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "Code ownership is an important concept in software development practices, and many developer portals now have a field where they require every project to have a “code owner”. But problems arise when everyone has a different definition of what being a code owner means. Not knowing who the owner is can cause confusion and friction in InnerSource projects. Questions that need answers are: Who is making architecture decisions for this project? Whose budget pays for this feature enhancement? Who do I call at 2am if the project is down? Who should get the credit for that amazing feature enhancement, achieved through an InnerSource contribution? Each case can be a different way of looking at code ownership. This lightning talk will examine what we mean when we talk about a “code owner” and will cover some of the many problems that inconsistent definitions within an organization can result in for your InnerSource practice.",
        "keywords": {
            "IEEE Keywords": [
                "Codes",
                "Friction",
                "Conferences",
                "Lightning",
                "Organizations",
                "Computer architecture",
                "Portals"
            ],
            "Index Terms": [
                "Software Development",
                "Inconsistent Definitions",
                "Software Quality",
                "Concept Of Ownership"
            ],
            "Author Keywords": [
                "InnerSource",
                "Open Source Software",
                "Code Ownership"
            ]
        }
    },
